 ## Snowmelt regime and trends {#sec-snowmelt}
 
-For every 1 m cell, we compiled 10 years of annual snowmelt DOY (2011–2021, excluding the missing year 2019) and calculated (i) **snowmelt climatology**, the 2011–2021 mean snowmelt date (DOY, day of year), which averages over interannual variation to represent the prevailing snowmelt timing at each location, and (ii) a per-pixel linear trend, the slope of an ordinary least-squares regression of DOY against year. As a perennial plant, *Sasa* is expected to respond to the prevailing local snowmelt regime rather than snowmelt in any single year, so both models used snowmelt climatology as the environmental predictor. Trends were not included as predictors. Per-pixel trend estimates are noisy, with a detection limit of approximately 2 days/year as discussed below, and adding the trend to Model B did not improve prediction in held-out spatial blocks (Supplementary Information).
